From 9c85ecb79e5e0c9860241a14d0c02c0afe61e77e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mathieu Gagne <mgagne@calavera.ca>
Date: Wed, 6 May 2026 21:09:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix interface config for neutronclient

endpoint_type is not recognized by openstacksdk.

[Bugfix cherry-picked from Ceilometer master branch]

neutron_client.py passes 'endpoint_type' when building the openstacksdk
Connection. Supplied directly as a kwarg it is silently discarded, and
the adapter falls back to the SDK default interface 'public', ignoring
service_credentials.interface = internal from ceilometer.conf.

As a result every pollster that reaches the Neutron API through
neutron_client.py targets the public endpoint, which does not resolve
from inside the pod network namespace, and is skipped on every polling
cycle:

  ip.floating
  network.services.vpn
  network.services.vpn.connections
  network.services.firewall
  network.services.firewall.policy

The per-instance interface counters (network.incoming.bytes and the
like) are unaffected, since the compute agent collects them via libvirt
without going through the Neutron API. The failure is independent of
TLS: it is an endpoint interface selection issue and affects both HTTP
and HTTPS deployments.

Cherry-pick of the upstream fix, merged to ceilometer master only and not
backported to stable/2026.1, so it is absent from the 26.0.0 (2026.1)
release. It is expected to ship in ceilometer 27.0.0 (2026.2), and this
patch should be retired once a version containing it is consumed.

  https://opendev.org/openstack/ceilometer/commit/9c85ecb79e5e0c9860241a14d0c02c0afe61e77e

Change-Id: If29c2cdb1c225f9f9c1e1422c4eacb82e5fa46fa
Signed-off-by: cbohlhal <Caique.BohlhalterdeSouza@windriver.com>
---
 ceilometer/neutron_client.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ceilometer/neutron_client.py b/ceilometer/neutron_client.py
index 7cf0fe480..087e691b8 100644
--- a/ceilometer/neutron_client.py
+++ b/ceilometer/neutron_client.py
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ class Client:
         creds = conf.service_credentials
         params = {
             'session': keystone_client.get_session(conf),
-            'endpoint_type': creds.interface,
+            'interface': creds.interface,
             'region_name': creds.region_name,
             'service_type': conf.service_types.neutron,
         }
-- 
